# SiteTracker backend — env file index.
#
# This is the generic template kept for discoverability. For real use,
# pick the per-environment example that matches your APP_ENV and copy
# it to the concrete (gitignored) filename:
#
#   cp .env.development.example .env.development     # local dev
#   cp .env.test.example        .env.test            # pytest target
#   cp .env.staging.example     .env.staging         # staging deploy
#   cp .env.production.example  .env.production      # production deploy
#
# Then edit values that need real secrets / hosts.
#
# Concrete .env.* files are gitignored (see /.gitignore). Only .example
# files are committed.
#
# Full var inventory, rotation procedure, and deployment promotion
# walkthrough live in docs/operations/env-and-secrets.md.
#
# APP_ENV is the canonical environment selector. ENVIRONMENT is a
# deprecated alias retained for one transitional release; setting both
# with different values fails fast on startup. See ADR 0002.
